From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:51:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: Add the RK3528 IEP2 deinterlacer

The RK3528's IEP2 deinterlaces with edge-directed interpolation, motion
detection and comb, OSD and pulldown detection, which mainline has no
driver for. Add a mem2mem driver taking an interlaced NV12 frame and
giving a progressive frame from each of its fields, as the sun8i
deinterlacer does on Allwinner, with the tuning Rockchip's MPP gives the
vendor kernel. It runs the I5O2 mode, motion read from the frames either
side: a frame goes back once it is no frame's previous, the first frame
stands in for its own previous, and on V4L2_DEC_CMD_STOP the last for
its own next, its second field's frame marked V4L2_BUF_FLAG_LAST. Each
stream keeps its own motion history, zeroed at its start, so a stream's
output does not depend on the one before it. The interrupt line is
shared with the VDPP and the IOMMU, so it is answered only while the
IEP is in use and in its own work mode.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
  drivers/media/platform/rockchip/Kconfig            |   1 +
  drivers/media/platform/rockchip/Makefile           |   1 +
  drivers/media/platform/rockchip/iep2/Kconfig       |  15 +
  drivers/media/platform/rockchip/iep2/Makefile      |   2 +
  .../platform/rockchip/iep2/rockchip-iep2-regs.h    | 118 +++
  .../media/platform/rockchip/iep2/rockchip-iep2.c   | 927 +++++++++++++++++++++
  6 files changed, 1064 insertions(+)

